Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Quantum Object Composition", "Title",
 CellID->509267359,ExpressionUUID->"22a1a762-10e3-861e-525e-3f4ca097ed64"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The public objects of ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumFramework"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4da796ef-9f57-a4bf-7b5c-0fc91ae30e85"],
 " \[LongDash] states, operators, channels, circuits, measurements, \
transforms \[LongDash] compose with one another via typed transformations: a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{
   "Q", "u", "a", "n", "t", "u", "m", "O", "p", "e", "r", "a", "t", "o", 
    "r"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1b39f900-6440-cee7-4ac6-f16a0dfa94cd"],
 " acting on a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"Q", "u", "a", "n", "t", "u", "m", "S", "t", "a", "t", "e"}], 
   "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "75d93363-5da6-51a4-23e6-ab4d5453238e"],
 " returns a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"Q", "u", "a", "n", "t", "u", "m", "S", "t", "a", "t", "e"}], 
   "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25a568a6-87a2-527f-535a-810032572145"],
 "; a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{
   "Q", "u", "a", "n", "t", "u", "m", "D", "i", "s", "t", "a", "n", "c", 
    "e"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "00d7f70d-8d0e-ae34-30ec-ef5724b8f51e"],
 " of two ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"Q", "u", "a", "n", "t", "u", "m", "S", "t", "a", "t", "e"}], 
   "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2f3e8453-9762-68ea-56c5-1e1d22173a30"],
 "s returns a real number. This tech note introduces a paclet-agnostic tool, \
Wolfram/PacletFunctionGraph, that introspects any paclet and produces a \
directed function-relation graph capturing exactly these compositions. After \
working through it, you will be able to read the type signature of every \
public symbol, distinguish type-preserving from type-changing morphisms, and \
render or query the composition graph for any neighborhood of interest."
}], "Text",
 CellID->329621944,ExpressionUUID->"5902d484-617f-9570-0f31-cdee100bfc5a"],

Cell["Loading the framework and building the graph", "Section",
 CellID->515379898,ExpressionUUID->"56e0e12c-de7d-6135-7e9f-f889db08301f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Load ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumFramework"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5708d032-2150-04f2-7d37-ca7c50e56ed8"],
 " and the Wolfram",
 Cell[BoxData["PacletFunctionGraph"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3b7807e8-9504-b25a-6907-9eb21cb600a0"],
 " helper paclet. The latter is not yet published, so we point \
PacletDirectoryLoad at the dev copy in this repository. The Remove call \
clears any Global",
 "`",
 " stubs interned by the front-end before the paclet was loaded, which would \
otherwise shadow the package's exports:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->604760901,ExpressionUUID->"166f8969-5e31-e8e5-3e14-21335bc5bacf"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<Wolfram`QuantumFramework`\>\"", "]"}], ";"}], 
  "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
  "PacletDirectoryLoad", "[", "\n", 
   "  ", "\"\<~/QuantumFramework/OngoingProjects/Improving doc \
pages/PacletFunctionGraph\>\"", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<Wolfram`PacletFunctionGraph`\>\"", "]"}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellID->1476799103,ExpressionUUID->"234f1fb7-07c6-bba9-5174-96f1b27009f3"],

Cell["\<\
Build the graph for QuantumFramework. BuildFunctionGraph loads the target \
paclet, walks its DownValues and SubValues to classify how every public \
symbol is called, and returns an Association keyed by symbol name. Predicate \
guards like _?QuantumStateQ or _?propQ are resolved automatically by walking \
each predicate's own DownValues \[LongDash] no manual configuration needed \
for any paclet:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->448336599,ExpressionUUID->"6ee45b93-a0df-d1f6-169c-52dcd16ba3dc"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"pacletRoot", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ParentDirectory", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"NotebookDirectory", "[", "]"}], ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"graphData", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"BuildFunctionGraph", "[", 
    RowBox[{"pacletRoot", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<WriteFile\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "False"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[1]:= ",
 CellID->970785311,ExpressionUUID->"0a3edd72-e0d3-62fb-3bc5-d53f916630c1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The result is an Association. A top-level ",
 Cell[BoxData["$Meta"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ec9a758-58be-624c-16f6-3f02594b3096"],
 " entry records when it was generated, the paclet identity, and any issues \
from generation:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1377816002,ExpressionUUID->"23253b8d-1c99-a6bf-52da-b2d7952d0c85"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"graphData", "[", "\"\<$Meta\>\"", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[2]:= ",
 CellID->1439899046,ExpressionUUID->"6e84829b-9667-6594-16bb-1bc523124ffe"],

Cell["\<\
Symbol entries (one per public head) populate the rest of the Association:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1641200340,ExpressionUUID->"569e173f-6b36-b240-7ea5-8f790ec000aa"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Keys", "[", 
  RowBox[{"KeyDrop", "[", 
   RowBox[{"graphData", ",", " ", "\"\<$Meta\>\""}], "]"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[3]:= ",
 CellID->1424533854,ExpressionUUID->"15a3e88e-0b57-fa6e-4350-01e8aee3c8b4"],

Cell["The type taxonomy", "Section",
 CellID->535457321,ExpressionUUID->"779c57de-bb93-d239-1da4-4e983e27a103"],

Cell["\<\
Every public head is classified into one of five Kinds. The Kind controls how \
the head fits into the composition picture:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->141959522,ExpressionUUID->"2867ea9b-6e8d-517b-581c-03c50b382041"],

Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "76dfbc62-92ac-7b6e-1ee4-364c275949b4"], Cell["Kind", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"0df4b6a5-173c-e15a-3b8b-2f0fa2ceb3a0"],
     Cell["Meaning", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"4d620fc7-5cf2-d9d8-7b11-a6a15484ab22"],
     Cell["Examples", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"741b091d-feb2-1a39-1c38-a146fb476903"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "3bf5a20e-c541-e06e-698a-446becf5b2b4"], Cell[
    "Constructor", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "07964fa7-8d1e-ff14-2dae-660124a8c27e"], Cell[
    "Builds an object of its own type from raw data.", "TableText",
     ExpressionUUID->"3e367b18-9aa8-58f9-67ce-73421f5d2ac3"], Cell[
    "QuantumState, QuantumBasis, QuantumMeasurement", "TableText",
     ExpressionUUID->"1dbaaaf7-1388-e538-4b59-43b1a622cc02"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "77d99fdb-a351-2d53-1de6-1684d6e477b9"], Cell[
    "Operator", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "04646437-faee-7dfc-2c1c-7e70fe9b47c6"], Cell["\<\
Object that also acts as a function on a target object, typically returning \
the same type.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"1cbde497-e826-5557-4442-fdd089d33fbd"], 
    Cell["QuantumOperator, QuantumChannel, QuantumCircuitOperator", 
     "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"6ecb37d0-fbcc-3e82-16c8-ae9dfe7e84e8"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "4c358d3e-86d3-ec5f-75ca-25783367b6a5"], Cell[
    "Transform", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "1f908cf3-3c70-d55a-45af-25bdb50abfa0"], Cell["\<\
Function that takes one object and returns the same or a related type.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"5dac66ba-272d-3627-0b54-7fe452d99d0d"], 
    Cell["\<\
QuantumPartialTrace, QuantumTensorProduct, QuantumWignerTransform\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"110914de-bbdd-83a1-4736-8d983e69d18b"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "76d004f9-29e5-6665-1eef-9da34f904d4f"], Cell[
    "Predicate", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "2c76c797-c249-79ca-540d-ded0f7fc4b10"], Cell[
    "Function returning a Boolean (Symbol True or False).", "TableText",
     ExpressionUUID->"35077f55-9291-6519-633d-771f27244c63"], Cell[
    "QuantumEntangledQ", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "4ebf3687-f906-130d-7644-afe0f8b37e57"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "65de4a87-3471-cd9f-13e6-63e1bd0597e5"], Cell[
    "Distance", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "7bedd9bd-1d84-ddaa-2992-d0e79436a7f0"], Cell[
    "Function returning a scalar (Real) from two states.", "TableText",
     ExpressionUUID->"4c37f35a-e1a6-07fe-75cc-eb0790536dc4"], Cell[
    "QuantumDistance, QuantumSimilarity", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "02f88238-86c8-66df-3287-2462337d4c25"]}
  }]], "3ColumnTableMod",
 CellID->299517738,ExpressionUUID->"034d641c-5834-e412-3173-7e4659c6cf78"],

Cell["Inspect the Kind distribution across the paclet:", "Text",
 CellID->2142391071,ExpressionUUID->"52ce4f6a-032d-a48b-02f6-6734b6d90ed1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"KeyValueMap", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"#1", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"#2", "[", "\"\<Kind\>\"", "]"}]}], "}"}], " ", "&"}], ",", 
    " ", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"KeyDrop", "[", 
     RowBox[{"graphData", ",", " ", "\"\<$Meta\>\""}], "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "//",
   " ", "TableForm"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[4]:= ",
 CellID->1002769646,ExpressionUUID->"5bfe104a-50de-a555-0985-8a1461680fbf"],

Cell["\<\
The Kind tag drives vertex coloring in the rendered graphs (next section) and \
is the first filter when querying for symbols of a given role. A \
\"Predicate\" head is, for example, never a source of any outgoing flow edge \
\[LongDash] it returns a scalar, not a paclet object.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->436346740,ExpressionUUID->"134534fb-1061-d656-417a-ada5a115bcbc"],

Cell["Reading an entry", "Section",
 CellID->2122865143,ExpressionUUID->"2cd98fd2-34e7-e188-54e6-269cbc93b3d2"],

Cell["\<\
Each symbol's entry records four fields: Kind, Accepts, OperatesOn, and \
ConsumedBy. Inspect QuantumState as an example:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1735808809,ExpressionUUID->"6e1c99a5-dcef-9c28-1623-100ed49be772"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"entry", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"graphData", "[", "\"\<QuantumState\>\"", "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Keys", "[", "entry", "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[5]:= ",
 CellID->753514147,ExpressionUUID->"608e87cc-8fce-afdf-10b5-1e962a78f525"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Accepts",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " is a list of input forms the head's constructor recognizes, classified by \
the WL ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"H", "e", "a", "d"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2aa912c6-4938-1bb7-5a56-8ba068cd699d"],
 " of the user-typed argument and tagged with a Role: \"Primary\" (the \
canonical input), \"Mutation\" (constructor takes its own head to re-wrap), \
\"Conversion\" (takes another paclet head and reroutes), \"NamedInstance\" (a \
String like \"Bell\" selecting a catalog entry), \"NamedArg\" (a Rule like \
\"Eigenvalues\" -> v), or \"PatternMachinery\" (internal). Tally the heads to \
see the dominant input forms:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1164297175,ExpressionUUID->"66b4bee0-d247-b105-0e4b-37cde7f3006f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Tally", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"#", "[", "\"\<Head\>\"", "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
   RowBox[{"entry", "[", "\"\<Accepts\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[6]:= ",
 CellID->632614636,ExpressionUUID->"337c2d89-644e-5b5e-6103-c4d30dfb29a4"],

Cell["\<\
Filter to just the entries whose Role is Primary or Conversion (the ones that \
produce graph edges):\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1689610856,ExpressionUUID->"5f7c2741-1c81-ec9b-0503-bf2b9535b6e1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Select", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"entry", "[", "\"\<Accepts\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"MemberQ", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<Primary\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<Mutation\>\"", ",", 
        " ", "\"\<Conversion\>\""}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"#", "[", "\"\<Role\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "&"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[7]:= ",
 CellID->1303163127,ExpressionUUID->"644cc522-c7c4-9b18-0c73-dc8ff276e662"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["OperatesOn",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " is non-",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"N", "o", "n", "e"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2de8c8f9-eaf3-8e90-5b97-e1a28e87d4fa"],
 " only for heads whose application has been recorded as F[args][target] in \
the kernel. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"Q", "u", "a", "n", "t", "u", "m", "S", "t", "a", "t", "e"}], 
   "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6801f052-da94-0b6f-183e-ea1fdf2159b5"],
 " is a Constructor, not an Operator, so this is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"N", "o", "n", "e"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0daf8e98-7628-e40b-3b54-27c203c2cf51"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->2098230307,ExpressionUUID->"7b6211f5-475c-1194-2911-88bf72e963fe"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"entry", "[", "\"\<OperatesOn\>\"", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[8]:= ",
 CellID->1930159659,ExpressionUUID->"7c8f7bdf-2493-8d8a-24b5-72994d27d7d0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["ConsumedBy",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " is the reverse-edge list: every other paclet symbol that takes ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"Q", "u", "a", "n", "t", "u", "m", "S", "t", "a", "t", "e"}], 
   "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "14e8dcaf-74c9-37ba-3c97-d5097d7d9d80"],
 " as input. This answers \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]what can I pass a state \
into?\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1113655915,ExpressionUUID->"5d5cbd3a-e88d-ee42-0b63-35678939b4a8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"entry", "[", "\"\<ConsumedBy\>\"", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[9]:= ",
 CellID->1606118752,ExpressionUUID->"3b7fe4cc-5889-7f4e-6904-fd96593c4594"],

Cell["Worked compositions", "Section",
 CellID->2141499446,ExpressionUUID->"6cb5c01f-62f5-68e0-144a-da5916803aca"],

Cell["\<\
The graph captures two structurally distinct kinds of composition. We walk \
through one example of each, then show a property-dispatch case that the \
graph deliberately does not record.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->339082558,ExpressionUUID->"55f417ec-7166-d78d-038b-8eb60010bdd7"],

Cell["Type-preserving: operator application", "Subsection",
 CellID->432388834,ExpressionUUID->"4b6e5dad-9702-0c1f-7916-54f722b75765"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "An ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"O", "p", "e", "r", "a", "t", "o", "r"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1d359769-845f-cd94-44ca-0f332deb97fe"],
 "-kind head applied to a target of type ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["T", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2055bfee-d4b5-7aa2-506a-36cbdd404888"],
 " typically returns a result of the same type ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["T", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "64c30c0d-1857-1b13-0cf0-a65799e26679"],
 ". In the flow graph this is a self-loop on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["T", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "46632a09-cc5f-b0ef-6e10-cc52e5eb0235"],
 ". Build a state, apply Pauli-X, and check the head:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->443736588,ExpressionUUID->"6ea251ed-865f-e03c-1652-48b733ebb306"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"state", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", "\"\<0\>\"", "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"operator", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", "\"\<X\>\"", "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"result", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"operator", "[", "state", "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Head", "[", "result", "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[10]:= ",
 CellID->1593449978,ExpressionUUID->"25a0bfbe-b1d4-2428-535f-36fbc0668f72"],

Cell["\<\
Same head as the target. That preservation is precisely the OperatesOn field \
of an Operator-kind head, recording \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]what target type, \
what output type\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] for each application form:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1742646261,ExpressionUUID->"04786d0e-016a-d127-2c07-8568b01ca00d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"graphData", "[", "\"\<QuantumOperator\>\"", "]"}], 
  "[", "\"\<OperatesOn\>\"", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[11]:= ",
 CellID->29467524,ExpressionUUID->"2d15b43a-cd49-5244-5b2a-2e67e4fc20ae"],

Cell["Type-changing: distance returns a Real", "Subsection",
 CellID->1939141443,ExpressionUUID->"2d1ff276-b82a-c3ca-5b24-f43039dc9110"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"D", "i", "s", "t", "a", "n", "c", "e"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "14fd1512-f616-8834-3c82-8d5f83a0db1e"],
 "-kind head consumes objects and produces a scalar. The composition is \
type-changing \[LongDash] from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"Q", "u", "a", "n", "t", "u", "m", "S", "t", "a", "t", "e"}], 
   "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "66c67103-72a1-9427-0efe-696d0755ff0d"],
 "s out to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"R", "e", "a", "l"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "48c794f4-84f6-2bfc-78fc-0dbe2c8379c6"],
 ". Because the graph drops scalars (Real / Integer / Boolean) from the node \
set, a Distance head appears as a vertex with only incoming edges (a sink):"
}], "Text",
 CellID->5047578,ExpressionUUID->"58ee7ecb-1370-1005-0896-7795a605636f"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"d", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"QuantumDistance", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", "\"\<0\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", "\"\<Plus\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", "\n", 
     "   ", "\"\<Fidelity\>\""}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Head", "[", 
  RowBox[{"N", "[", "d", "]"}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[12]:= ",
 CellID->15008895,ExpressionUUID->"11d04a92-cbef-a8a5-47e0-63dfed9bfa8f"],

Cell["\<\
QuantumDistance's Accepts list confirms it consumes QuantumStates and a \
metric-name String:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1892712309,ExpressionUUID->"7d9821c9-0e61-bc6d-2ba7-b893ab1506b7"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"graphData", "[", "\"\<QuantumDistance\>\"", "]"}], 
  "[", "\"\<Accepts\>\"", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[13]:= ",
 CellID->787969749,ExpressionUUID->"3181a460-bc62-f1ee-67be-3e4a3514c334"],

Cell["Property dispatch (not captured by the graph)", "Subsection",
 CellID->525088789,ExpressionUUID->"3937e1d4-04c3-e55a-68cc-f89ead77cfa0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Every paclet object responds to property-string queries: qs[\"DensityMatrix\
\"] returns a matrix, qs[\"NormalizedState\"] returns a fresh ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"Q", "u", "a", "n", "t", "u", "m", "S", "t", "a", "t", "e"}], 
   "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6b45e796-37a7-eecc-197a-fed04253b416"],
 ", and so on. These are runtime accessors, not constructor calls, so they \
don't appear as edges in the function-graph by design \[LongDash] the graph \
is about ",
 StyleBox["object-to-object", "TI"],
 " composition, not property lookup. Still, the writer of a ref page \
documents them; here is a quick survey on a Bell state:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->357930410,ExpressionUUID->"5e187950-8ca2-2ab2-0638-711a25577898"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"qs", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", "\"\<PhiPlus\>\"", "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Head", "[", 
    RowBox[{"qs", "[", "\"\<DensityMatrix\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Head", "[", 
    RowBox[{"qs", "[", "\"\<NormalizedState\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Head", "[", 
    RowBox[{"qs", "[", "\"\<VonNeumannEntropy\>\"", "]"}], "]"}]}], 
  "}"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[14]:= ",
 CellID->1802489801,ExpressionUUID->"250a2d7c-9b81-05b0-5309-c5261e346f9a"],

Cell["Rendering the graph", "Section",
 CellID->115301326,ExpressionUUID->"15a9104d-5625-6af3-4356-8a1763d038d9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Three rendering helpers ship with Wolfram",
 Cell[BoxData["PacletFunctionGraph"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "58c17d8b-1b7e-6f79-08ff-74d59e0b3243"],
 ": PacletFlowEdges (the edge primitive), SymbolNeighborhoodGraph (one \
symbol's flow neighborhood), and PacletOverviewGraph (the whole paclet). All \
three accept the graph Association and return either an edge list or a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"G", "r", "a", "p", "h"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "43821c38-6720-b4f9-71b1-966212da1ec3"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1651187567,ExpressionUUID->"341c54d9-3079-6bba-5c24-4d83410c3980"],

Cell["\<\
The flow neighborhood of QuantumState: every incoming arrow is a head that \
flows into QuantumState (as constructor input or as the output of an operator \
that produces a state), and every outgoing arrow is a head that consumes a \
QuantumState. The bold black border marks the focal vertex; node color \
encodes Kind.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->941376513,ExpressionUUID->"1dbf9c2b-d84a-d79b-4b44-1674d9fcbde1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"SymbolNeighborhoodGraph", "[", 
  RowBox[{"graphData", ",", " ", "\"\<QuantumState\>\""}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[15]:= ",
 CellID->2120243592,ExpressionUUID->"0f449897-1a0e-51e7-357b-11d19fbb23cd"],

Cell["\<\
The paclet-wide flow view. Operator-like heads (green) cluster in the upper \
rows with self-loops indicating they preserve their target type; Transforms \
(yellow) sit one layer below; Distance / Predicate / Similarity (purple / \
red) are pure sinks with only incoming arrows:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1047559317,ExpressionUUID->"6d5a63ab-93b9-14f3-1b7a-7af5264c7ed9"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"PacletOverviewGraph", "[", "graphData", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[16]:= ",
 CellID->1820947576,ExpressionUUID->"5077c06e-c394-b43c-000c-da4bf6261f06"],

Cell["\<\
If you only want the raw edge data, PacletFlowEdges returns a deduplicated \
list of {from, to} pairs. This is useful when feeding the graph into other \
tooling (e.g. computing centrality or partitioning):\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->670734585,ExpressionUUID->"07359582-e823-44a1-2eca-0cef89d62e8b"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"edges", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PacletFlowEdges", "[", "graphData", "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Length", "[", "edges", "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Take", "[", 
    RowBox[{"edges", ",", " ", "5"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[17]:= ",
 CellID->58232708,ExpressionUUID->"7c239bd0-3ff5-3b18-25d0-129ab9818662"],

Cell["Querying the graph", "Section",
 CellID->393464600,ExpressionUUID->"68c76573-72ce-0c1a-18fd-7d3d077b5760"],

Cell["\<\
The graph is data \[LongDash] queryable with standard Association/list \
patterns.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1484396876,ExpressionUUID->"6184d2f2-049e-728e-17bb-cbbcad2b40d4"],

Cell["What produces a QuantumState?", "Subsection",
 CellID->1149283354,ExpressionUUID->"4fd967ef-5008-0b29-75e7-7ec961bd5673"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Find the symbols with an outgoing edge into ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"Q", "u", "a", "n", "t", "u", "m", "S", "t", "a", "t", "e"}], 
   "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "19bb1c5e-57ab-6e36-4f58-9618625e351c"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1092188694,ExpressionUUID->"5c8dcc56-7aa9-964a-04b2-e6107f5dfc90"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"producers", " ", "=", " ", "\n", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Cases", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"PacletFlowEdges", "[", "graphData", "]"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"f_", ",", " ", "\"\<QuantumState\>\""}], "}"}], " ", ":>", " ",
      "f"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[18]:= ",
 CellID->559599970,ExpressionUUID->"30baa1c8-66ad-75e0-6059-389213585fca"],

Cell["What consumes a QuantumState?", "Subsection",
 CellID->1710123944,ExpressionUUID->"52535901-cb26-8b9c-0261-516aeed0d9e6"],

Cell["\<\
The mirror query: outgoing edges from QuantumState. Equivalent to (but easier \
to read than) the symmetric look-up in ConsumedBy:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->934597701,ExpressionUUID->"323a4b1c-b138-a791-63da-6359c0b20dfb"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"consumers", " ", "=", " ", "\n", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Cases", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"PacletFlowEdges", "[", "graphData", "]"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<QuantumState\>\"", ",", " ", "t_"}], "}"}], " ", ":>", " ",
      "t"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[19]:= ",
 CellID->284780108,ExpressionUUID->"7421cf44-a1ac-4319-1dde-e721d0592e63"],

Cell["Which heads are closed under their own action?", "Subsection",
 CellID->643798763,ExpressionUUID->"511b3347-8d7d-ab60-0738-ab212409f64a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "An operator-like head is closed if its OperatesOn maps some paclet head ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["K", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "36c19c85-764d-0b01-5efe-15ef03f8566b"],
 " back to itself \[LongDash] in the flow graph, a self-loop or a parallel \
pair ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["K", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6815cd54-0cd7-196f-182a-e51ea5626bb5"],
 " -> ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["F", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "519775d4-d545-25f2-07ad-6c91dcf18fd8"],
 " -> ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["K", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5900aac7-5263-773e-0f3f-43a167165a04"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->268959046,ExpressionUUID->"06ecfdb3-2197-c9b0-2e93-f4fd50239b9a"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"selfLoops", "[", "g_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Cases", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"PacletFlowEdges", "[", "g", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"x_", ",", " ", "x_"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"selfLoops", "[", "graphData", "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[20]:= ",
 CellID->403125484,ExpressionUUID->"12d95fcb-3316-2212-42e7-569546a37178"],

Cell["Which heads are sinks?", "Subsection",
 CellID->931950651,ExpressionUUID->"733995c2-f5bf-78ee-22c6-0caffc4a4a34"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A sink has incoming edges but no outgoing ones \[LongDash] symbols whose \
output is a scalar (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"R", "e", "a", "l"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4f8ab258-7e7f-0723-7589-34027b0a6a09"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"B", "o", "o", "l", "e", "a", "n"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6b12ee74-9953-131d-1921-003e18e67e67"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"A", "s", "s", "o", "c", "i", "a", "t", "i", "o", "n"}], "TI"]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "65262d3c-fccc-1dc6-0cdd-c579f579672c"],
 ") rather than a paclet object. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{
   "Q", "u", "a", "n", "t", "u", "m", "D", "i", "s", "t", "a", "n", "c", 
    "e"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5e157ee2-48da-d240-062b-77cc696ca0aa"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{
   "Q", "u", "a", "n", "t", "u", "m", "E", "n", "t", "a", "n", "g", "l", "e", 
    "d", "Q"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "78287f93-0f12-7c52-2828-76ddaaa746b8"],
 " are typical sinks:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->412518898,ExpressionUUID->"08285353-0e0e-39f8-3828-4b1dabb88bc2"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"sinks", "[", "g_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"e", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"PacletFlowEdges", "[", "g", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
     "     ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Complement", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"e", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", 
          RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"e", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", 
          RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "//", 
      " ", "Union"}]}], "\n", "   ", "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"sinks", "[", "graphData", "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[21]:= ",
 CellID->622967176,ExpressionUUID->"1daed7d3-93e8-7698-4b55-ce9d259d5ce2"],

Cell["Where this leaves us", "Section",
 CellID->1358080856,ExpressionUUID->"187adc3d-3961-76c2-4819-d667b8145c28"],

Cell["Three takeaways:", "Text",
 CellID->320615307,ExpressionUUID->"641c78eb-7f03-7846-0c24-71b57ab64aac"],

Cell["\<\
\[Bullet] Every public QuantumFramework head has a typed signature recorded \
in the function-graph. The composition rules are not buried in kernel files \
\[LongDash] one call to BuildFunctionGraph produces a queryable Association.\
\>", "Item",
 CellID->1594238871,ExpressionUUID->"5bfcc75d-c21d-6fb0-0983-df06f7a8359a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\[Bullet] Operator-like heads are characterized by self-loops in the flow \
graph (their OperatesOn maps their target type back to itself). ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{
   "Q", "u", "a", "n", "t", "u", "m", "O", "p", "e", "r", "a", "t", "o", 
    "r"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "112ae6ec-4b5c-6ad2-4729-ffb66ee93838"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{
   "Q", "u", "a", "n", "t", "u", "m", "C", "h", "a", "n", "n", "e", "l"}], 
   "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6121b9de-dddd-aca8-10de-309bd469f6f2"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{
   "Q", "u", "a", "n", "t", "u", "m", "C", "i", "r", "c", "u", "i", "t", "O", 
    "p", "e", "r", "a", "t", "o", "r"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "30209679-023a-ee91-61df-0823b7ccb4fb"],
 " all preserve ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"Q", "u", "a", "n", "t", "u", "m", "S", "t", "a", "t", "e"}], 
   "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "29bc1606-c22d-409d-5f43-8863f7d812e7"],
 " under application."
}], "Item",
 CellID->2002505366,ExpressionUUID->"7bf1e1bf-5b3e-c64b-298e-f8f95ec8ac91"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\[Bullet] Type-changing heads (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{
   "Q", "u", "a", "n", "t", "u", "m", "D", "i", "s", "t", "a", "n", "c", 
    "e"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3119d855-3ffd-7401-6726-d21fb9885f6b"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{
   "Q", "u", "a", "n", "t", "u", "m", "E", "n", "t", "a", "n", "g", "l", "e", 
    "d", "Q"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "62a6d1b5-4e36-fa69-125d-c8ff6bc0c8b3"],
 ") return scalars and therefore appear as sink vertices: incoming edges only."
}], "Item",
 CellID->2121396920,ExpressionUUID->"7c41cdc9-5ab3-1ef5-247e-e4935f4664df"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The same workflow applies to any paclet: Needs[\"Wolfram",
 Cell[BoxData["PacletFunctionGraph"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "51fce014-dca1-0630-0783-fa51d5546d1a"],
 "\"], BuildFunctionGraph[\"/path/to/SomePaclet\"], then render or query."
}], "Text",
 CellID->993357154,ExpressionUUID->"657c1c65-980e-511d-1303-964f19bb2067"],

